[38.596252, "o", "# Stripe - last 30 days\r\nCache: MISS_COLD\r\n\r\n## News\r\n- Stripe cofounder John Collison hosted Meta executives Mark Zuckerberg and Alexandr Wang on the \"Cheeky Pint\" podcast to discuss Meta's AI ambitions and spending plans. [S2, S6, 18d old]\r\n- Mark Zuckerberg stated that demand for Meta's Muse was high enough to require Stripe to raise credit limits. [S7, 15d old]\r\n- Stripe is collaborating with FedEx Dataworks to use supply chain intelligence to provide financing for small and medium-sized businesses. [S11, S13, 10d old]\r\n- Stripe plans to acquire the embedded financial products platform Parafin to strengthen its support for platforms. [S11, 10d old]\r\n\r\n## Hires\r\n  (nothing sourced in this window)\r\n\r\n## Launches\r\n- Stripe launched Link Balance, a product that provides autonomous AI agents with balances, currently available to US customers. [S4, 6d old]\r\n- Stripe Treasury has been launched in the UK, allowing founders to manage money from a single dashboard. [S5, 4d old]\r\n- Stripe and Plasma are co-developing a multi-currency card experience that allows users to spend across multiple balances. [S8, S11, 10d old]\r\n- Stripe launched Treasury for agents, which allows startups to manage financial operations using AI agents. [S12, 15d old]\r\n- Stripe unveiled Stripe Pay, a tool designed to facilitate B2B payments. [S10, 10d old]\r\n\r\n## Questions to ask (suggestions)\r\n- How does the integration with FedEx Dataworks change the risk assessment process for SMB financing?\r\n- What are the security implications of allowing AI agents to manage financial operations via Stripe Treasury?\r\n- How does the multi-currency card partnership with Plasma fit into Stripe's broader strategy for business money movement?\r\n- What specific metrics or thresholds triggered the need to raise credit limits for Meta's Muse users?\r\n\r\n## Sources\r\nS1. Seattle's I-5 construction headache is ending early — for now - Axios (2026-10-28) https://axios.com/local/seattle/2026/10/28/i5-seattle-ship-canal-bridge-lane-closures-end-2026\r\nS2. Mark Zuckerberg and Alexandr Wang don't seem to like Guinness very much - Business Insider (2026-10-13) https://businessinsider.com/mark-zuckerberg-and-alexandr-wang-dont-seem-sold-on-guinness-2026-10\r\nS3. United CEO Scott Kirby says he had an 'epiphany' after hiring an AI tutor and vibe-coding a sports betting tool - Business Insider (2026-10-27) https://businessinsider.com/united-ceo-scott-kirby-ai-tutor-vibe-coded-gambling-tool-2026-10\r\nS4. Deep Dive: How Stripe's Link gives AI agents money they ... (2026-11-01) https://finextra.com/blogposting/33362/deep-dive-how-stripes-link-gives-ai-agents-money-they-can-spend\r\nS5. Stripe Treasury launches in the UK (2026-11-03) https://finextra.com/pressarticle/111563/stripe-treasury-launches-in-the-uk\r\nS6. Zuckerberg spent years building on Apple’s terms. His $100 billion-plus AI bet is about owning everything - Fortune (2026-10-20) https://fortune.com/2026/10/20/zuckerberg-apple-lesson-meta-100-billion-ai-bet\r\nS7. Mark Zuckerberg said demand for Meta’s Muse was so high, he had to get Stripe to raise credit limits - Fortune (2026-10-22) https://fortune.com/2026/10/22/mark-zuckerberg-meta-muse-stripe-credit-limit-shopping\r\nS8. Stripe and Plasma co-develop a new multi-currency card experience | Markets Insider (2026-10-15) https://markets.businessinsider.com/news/stocks/stripe-and-plasma-co-develop-a-new-multi-currency-card-experience-1036630108\r\nS9. Stripe agentic commerce revs up (2026-10-15) https://paymentsdive.com/news/stripe-agentic-commerce-revs-up/833109\r\nS10. Stripe Unveils B2B Payments that Mirror the P2P Experience - PaymentsJournal (2026-10-28) https://paymentsjournal.com/stripe-unveils-b2b-payments-that-mirror-the-p2p-experience\r\nS11. PYMNTS | Stripe Pay Targets Instant B2B Payments (2026-10-28) https://pymnts.com/news/b2b-payments/2026/stripe-pay-targets-instant-b2b-payments\r\nS12. Stripe launches Treasury for AI agents | The Paypers (2026-10-23) https://thepaypers.com/fintech/news/stripe-launches-treasury-for-agents-to-automate-startup-finances\r\nS13. FedEx and Stripe team "]
